the champions league final is one of the  biggest events on the global sporting  calendar  hosting the match brings prestige and  tourism among other benefits  paris will now host this season's final  after saint petersburg was stripped of  the honour by european football's  governing body uefa  they've also decided russian and  ukrainian club and national teams are to  play home games at neutral venues  fifa will have to decide whether or not  russia's world cup play-off in moscow  next month against poland will go ahead  as planned fifa has already spoken out  against the conflict  fifa expresses  hope for  a rapid  cessation  of hostilities  and for peace  in  ukraine  fifa condemns as well  the use of force  by russia in ukraine  and any type  of violence to resolve conflicts  meanwhile manchester united have  cancelled their 10-year sponsorship deal  with russia's national airline aeroflot  the airline had been united's official  carrier since 2013 and the deal was  thought to be worth more than 53 million  dollars  football is not the only sport taking  action formula one has cancelled this  season's russian grand prix the race was  due to be held on september 25th in  sochi f1 drivers are backing the  decision to boycott russia  like everyone said you know innocent  people  losing their lives you know people  losing their homes and and families and  don't have safe places to to live in  it's it's not right but well we can hope  that everything gets resolved in the  best possible outcome and way that is  that is possible and for now i think is  the right decision by  formula one not to go to russia but  ukraine has also been hit the national  basketball team's home match in kiev  against spain has had to be postponed  russian tennis star andre rublev made  clear his views on the matter after a  win in dubai on friday but unless there  is a swift end to the conflict more  sporting events are likely to be  postponed cancelled or moved to neutral  venues peter samut al jazeera
 

